[size=12pt][b][url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/releases/download/v0.1.1/crew-stations-0.1.1.zip]Download v0.1.1 (beta)[/url][/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations]Source code on GitHub[/url] | [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/releases]All releases[/url]

[b]Requires:[/b] Starsector 0.98a. [b]No other mods needed.[/b][/center]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]Save compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[li][b]Can be added to an ongoing game:[/b] yes.[/li]
[li][b]Can be removed:[/b] [color=orange]no.[/color] Ships with Stations carry the Crew Stations hullmod, and a save that has them needs the mod to load. Keep a backup.[/li]
[li][b]Other mods:[/b] compatible. Works with modded ships and modded heavy industries. Tested with Nexerelin, Exotica Technologies and Random Assortment of Things.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]A message from Station Yard Inc.[/b][/size]
[i]Tired of crews who merely survive? [b]Station Yard Inc.[/b], the Sector's most exclusive outfitter, fits your ships with hand-crafted crewed Stations: shield control rooms, engine rooms, missile magazines and more, staffed by the finest specialists money can rent. Visit any of our showrooms, conveniently located wherever there is heavy industry. Prices are high because quality is high. Also because we can.[/i]
[size=8pt]Station Yard Inc. is not responsible for crew lost to vacuum, pirates or the Domain. Warranty void if boarded. Financing not available in your sector.[/size]

[size=12pt][b]What the mod actually does[/b][/size]
Dock at any market with heavy industry and visit the [b]Station Yard Inc. showroom[/b]. There you can build dedicated, crewed compartments aboard your ships: a shield control room, an engine room, a missile magazine... Each Station improves one part of the ship and can be upgraded twice. They are expensive, they need extra crew, and they stay with the ship for good.

[b]How it works[/b]
[list]
[li][b]Find a Shipyard:[/b] any market with working Heavy Industry whose owner is not hostile, your own colonies included. The dock menu shows [i]Visit the Station Yard Inc. showroom[/i].[/li]
[li][b]Pick a ship:[/b] frigates have 1 Station slot, destroyers 2, cruisers 3, capitals 4. Automated ships have no crew, so no Stations.[/li]
[li][b]Order a Station[/b] from the Catalogue: ten types, each with its own requirement (shields, a phase cloak, fighter bays, the right weapon slot...).[/li]
[li][b]Upgrade it:[/b] Standard, Deluxe, Platinum. Platinum needs a showroom with Orbital Works or a nanoforge.[/li]
[li][b]Pay for it:[/b] credits plus heavy machinery, metals and rare metals, taken from your cargo, then your storage there, then the open market. Bigger hulls pay more.[/li]
[/list]
Every Station level adds 10% to the ship's skeleton and max crew. A Station whose requirement is no longer met (shields turned into Shield Shunt, say) goes inactive: no bonus, crew still needed. Dismantling refunds 25% of the credits (the rest is a restocking fee, naturally).

[center][img width=800]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/main/docs/assets/picker.png[/img]
[i]The Catalogue: every Station, its effects at all three levels, and exactly where the materials will come from.[/i][/center]

[spoiler=The ten Stations (level 1 / 2 / 3)]
[list]
[li][b]Shield Station[/b] (needs shields): shield damage taken -5/10/15%, turn and unfold rate +15/30/50%, upkeep -10/20/30%[/li]
[li][b]Logistics Station:[/b] supplies per month -5/10/15%, fuel use -10/20/30%[/li]
[li][b]Engine Station:[/b] top speed +5/10/15%, acceleration, deceleration and turn rate +15/30/50%[/li]
[li][b]Energy Station[/b] (needs an energy slot): energy weapon damage +3/6/10%, energy flux cost -5/10/15%[/li]
[li][b]Ballistic Station[/b] (needs a ballistic slot): rate of fire +5/10/15%, ballistic flux cost -5/10/15%[/li]
[li][b]Missile Silo[/b] (needs a missile slot): missile ammo +25/50/100%, missile hitpoints +15/30/50%, reload rate +15/30/50%[/li]
[li][b]Phase Station[/b] (needs a phase cloak): phase upkeep -10/20/30%, phase cooldown -10/20/30%[/li]
[li][b]Reactor Station:[/b] flux capacity +5/10/15%, flux dissipation +5/10/15%[/li]
[li][b]Damage Control Station:[/b] hull damage taken -5/10/15%, weapon and engine repairs +25/50/75%, crew lost -25/50/75%[/li]
[li][b]Flight Deck[/b] (needs fighter bays): fighter replacement time -10/20/30%, fighter top speed +5/10/15%[/li]
[li][b]Simulator Bay[/b] (reward, see below): max combat readiness +5/10/15, CR recovery +15/30/50%[/li]
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/main/docs/assets/hullmod-tooltip.png[/img]
[i]The Crew Stations hullmod lists every Station and its crew cost in the refit screen.[/i][/center]
[/spoiler]

[spoiler=Prices]
For a destroyer. Frigates pay x0.5, cruisers x2, capitals x4 (credits and materials).
[list]
[li][b]Level 1:[/b] 112,500 credits, 75 heavy machinery[/li]
[li][b]Level 2:[/b] 300,000 credits, 150 heavy machinery, 375 metals[/li]
[li][b]Level 3:[/b] 675,000 credits, 225 heavy machinery, 150 rare metals[/li]
[/list]
A capital with four Platinum Stations is a late-game project on purpose. Station Yard Inc. thanks you for your business.
[/spoiler]

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]A reward for Descent veterans[/b][/size]
Won a Run in [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/slay_the_sector]Slay the Sector[/url]? Station Yard Inc. has heard, and adds the [b]Simulator Bay[/b] to its Catalogue: as an exceptional pilot, you stream your combat exploits to boost crew morale. No one has to know it was a simulation. Any save, any faction, normal price. Neither mod needs the other.

[hr]

[size=12pt][b]This is a beta[/b][/size]
Everything in the mod works, but it is still being polished:
[list]
[li][b]Balance is a first pass.[/b] Some Stations may feel too strong or too weak, and prices too cheap or too expensive. Your feedback is exactly what will fix that.[/li]
[li][b]Bugs are possible.[/b] Known: a ship sold to a market keeps its Stations if you buy it back.[/li]
[/list]
[b]Found a problem, or something felt off?[/b] Please tell me! The easiest way is the [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/issues/new/choose]Report a problem page[/url] on GitHub: pick "Report a bug" or "Balance feedback", and a short form guides you (you only need a free GitHub account). Describe what happened in your own words. If you can, drag and drop the file [b]starsector.log[/b] from your Starsector folder into the form: it helps a lot.
Replies in this thread are welcome too.

Every number (effects, slots, crew cost, prices, the level 3 rule) can also be changed in [b]data/config/settings.json[/b], if you like to tinker. With Console Commands installed, the [b]crst[/b] command lists, adds and clears Stations.

[hr]

[spoiler=Changelog]
[b]0.1.1 (beta)[/b]
[list]
[li]The shop is now run by [b]Station Yard Inc.[/b], a luxurious megacorp: a showroom at every Shipyard, a slogan of the day, The Catalogue, signed orders and a restocking fee on returns.[/li]
[li]Levels are now Standard, Deluxe and Platinum.[/li]
[/list]

[b]0.1.0 (beta)[/b]
First public release: ten Station types with three levels, Shipyards at heavy industry markets, the Station Yard Inc. showroom, the Crew Stations hullmod, and full configuration in settings.json.

Full history in the [url=https://github.com/PaulRouss3l/crew_stations/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]changelog[/url].
[/spoiler]

